         ```bash                                                                
         sed -i 's/("127.0.0.1", 8765)/("0.0.0.0", 8765)/'                      
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface_bind_address/server.py                                        
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         2. Build the image so the updated server.py is included. Use Minikube's
         image build if your kubectl context is minikube; otherwise build with  
         docker.                                                                
         ```bash                                                                
         IMAGE=kube-wrong-interface-bind-address-app:latest                     
         DOCKERFILE=/home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshoot
         ing/wrong_interface_bind_address/Dockerfile                            
         CONTEXT=/home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting
         /wrong_interface_bind_address                                          
                                                                                
         if kubectl config current-context | grep -qi minikube; then            
           PROFILE=${MINIKUBE_PROFILE:-$(kubectl config current-context)}       
           minikube -p "$PROFILE" image build -t "$IMAGE" -f "$DOCKERFILE"      
         "$CONTEXT"                                                             
         else                                                                   
           docker build -t "$IMAGE" -f "$DOCKERFILE" "$CONTEXT"                 
         fi                                                                     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         3. Replace the running Pod with the rebuilt image (delete and reapply  
         the Pod manifest). This ensures the cluster runs the updated image     
         (imagePullPolicy: Never will use the locally-built image).             
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl delete -f                                                      
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface_bind_address/wrong_interface_bind_address.yaml                
         --ignore-not-found                                                     
         kubectl apply -f                                                       
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface_bind_address/wrong_interface_bind_address.yaml                
         kubectl wait --for=condition=ready                                     
         pod/kube-wrong-interface-bind-address --timeout=60s                    
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         4. Verify the application is reachable through the Service (cluster    
         DNS) and directly inside the Pod.                                      
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl run --rm -i --restart=Never test-curl --image=curlimages/curl  
         --command -- sh -c 'curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n"          
         http://wrong-interface-bind-address-service:8000/'                     
                                                                                
         kubectl exec kube-wrong-interface-bind-address -- python3 -c "import   
